WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.115
Risk informs where the design review needs
depth.

2
00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:08.013
In our fictional case, a missing mixing
protection can permit transfer after

3
00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:12.805
loss of agitation, potentially affecting
concentration uniformity.

4
00:00:12.925 --> 00:00:16.275
Explain that mechanism before assigning a
priority.

5
00:00:16.395 --> 00:00:20.747
Another issue, such as an inconsistent
drawing title, may primarily

6
00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:22.573
affect document control.

7
00:00:22.693 --> 00:00:26.000
Both require action, but their
consequences differ.

8
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:30.557
A risk label without an explanation gives
the reviewer little basis for

9
00:00:30.677 --> 00:00:32.768
deciding what evidence is enough.

10
00:00:33.388 --> 00:00:37.335
A numerical risk score can organize
discussion but cannot

11
00:00:37.455 --> 00:00:39.012
supply missing knowledge.

12
00:00:39.132 --> 00:00:42.481
This lesson uses no universal score
threshold.

13
00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:46.953
If a serious failure has weak evidence for
prevention or detection, keep

14
00:00:47.073 --> 00:00:51.212
that uncertainty visible even when an
arithmetic total looks small.

15
00:00:51.332 --> 00:00:55.087
Review assumptions, operating conditions
and dependencies.

16
00:00:55.207 --> 00:00:59.943
Do not reduce a risk rating merely because
a proposed control appears on the

17
00:01:00.063 --> 00:01:04.372
drawing; its effectiveness still needs
support and later verification.

18
00:01:04.992 --> 00:01:09.728
For the mixing scenario, the proposed
control inhibits transfer when loss of

19
00:01:09.848 --> 00:01:11.725
agitation is detected.

20
00:01:11.845 --> 00:01:16.560
Review sensor coverage, logic, bypass
authority and reset behaviour.

21
00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.140
Ask whether the sensing arrangement could
miss the failure being considered.

22
00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.015
Link the design response to a planned
controlled challenge of

23
00:01:25.135 --> 00:01:26.628
the protective function.

24
00:01:26.748 --> 00:01:31.356
The teaching diagram shows failure,
control and verification as connected

25
00:01:31.476 --> 00:01:35.615
steps, not as proof that any specific
interlock is already effective.

26
00:01:36.235 --> 00:01:40.608
A useful risk-informed review records what
remains uncertain, who will

27
00:01:40.728 --> 00:01:43.720
resolve it and what change triggers
another review.

28
00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.469
For example, a later product with
different viscosity may invalidate the

29
00:01:48.589 --> 00:01:50.424
original mixing assumption.

30
00:01:50.544 --> 00:01:53.829
Keep that trigger linked to the
requirements and design.

31
00:01:53.949 --> 00:01:58.813
Your activity is to compare two design
findings and justify the depth of

32
00:01:58.933 --> 00:02:00.223
review for each.

33
00:02:00.343 --> 00:02:04.610
Do not force every question into a
numerical ranking when a reasoned

34
00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.394
explanation is clearer.
